---
import SubPage from '../../layouts/SubPage.astro';
import { DOCS_SIDEBAR } from '../../lib/sidebar-data';
import {
  CONNECTOR_CATEGORIES,
  CONNECTOR_GROUP_ORDER,
  CONNECTOR_GROUP_LABELS,
} from '../../lib/connector-data';

const currentPath = '/docs/connectors';

const grouped: Record<string, typeof CONNECTOR_CATEGORIES> = {};
for (const g of CONNECTOR_GROUP_ORDER) grouped[g] = [];
for (const c of CONNECTOR_CATEGORIES) {
  grouped[c.group].push(c);
}
---

<SubPage
  title="Connectors · Pace"
  description="How Pace plugins connect to your real tools (Slack, HubSpot, Snowflake, Notion, Linear, and dozens more) through the Model Context Protocol. Install flow, OAuth authorization, swappable connectors, and the full category catalog."
  activeNav="docs"
  canonicalPath={currentPath}
  sidebarLabel="Docs"
>
  <Fragment slot="sidebar">
    {DOCS_SIDEBAR.map((group) => (
      <div class="subpage-sidebar-group">
        <span class="subpage-sidebar-group-title">{group.title}</span>
        <ul class="subpage-sidebar-list">
          {group.items.map((item) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={item.href}
                aria-current={item.href === currentPath ? 'page' : undefined}
              >{item.label}</a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </Fragment>

  <article class="connectors-page">
    <header class="connectors-header">
      <span class="connectors-eyebrow">Reference</span>
      <h1>Connectors</h1>
      <p class="connectors-lede">
        Connectors wire Claude to the external tools your role depends on: CRMs, project trackers, data warehouses, design tools, and more. They use the <a href="https://modelcontextprotocol.io/">Model Context Protocol (MCP)</a>. Every pace plugin ships with a <code>.mcp.json</code> listing the MCP servers it can use; install the plugin and the connectors come along.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="connectors-section" id="installing">
      <h2>Installing</h2>
      <p>Connectors install along with the plugin. There's no separate connector install step.</p>

      <pre class="connectors-pre"><code><span class="connectors-comment"># 1. Register the marketplace once</span>
claude plugin marketplace add pace.tools

<span class="connectors-comment"># 2. Install a plugin (its .mcp.json registers connectors)</span>
claude plugin install sales@pace.tools</code></pre>

      <p>After the plugin install, the connectors are <strong>declared but not yet authorized</strong>. Authorization happens on first use, per MCP server, via OAuth in your browser.</p>

      <h3>The <code>.mcp.json</code> manifest</h3>
      <p>Each plugin's <code>.mcp.json</code> at its directory root lists the MCP servers. For example, <code>plugins/sales/.mcp.json</code> looks like this:</p>

      <pre class="connectors-pre"><code>&#123;
  "mcpServers": &#123;
    "slack":   &#123; "type": "http", "url": "https://mcp.slack.com/mcp" &#125;,
    "hubspot": &#123; "type": "http", "url": "https://mcp.hubspot.com/anthropic" &#125;,
    "notion":  &#123; "type": "http", "url": "https://mcp.notion.com/mcp" &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

      <p>That's the whole config. Vendors host the MCP server at the URL; users authorize via OAuth. You don't manage API keys yourself.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="connectors-section" id="authorizing">
      <h2>Authorizing</h2>
      <p>Three flavors of authorization, depending on the connector type.</p>

      <h3>OAuth (most connectors)</h3>
      <p>For hosted MCP servers (Slack, HubSpot, Notion, Asana, Linear, etc.), Claude triggers an OAuth flow on first use:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>You run a skill that needs the connector. Example: <code>/sales:call-prep Acme</code> needs HubSpot.</li>
        <li>Claude detects the connector isn't authorized yet and opens an OAuth URL in your browser.</li>
        <li>You sign in to the vendor and approve Pace's access scope.</li>
        <li>The browser redirects back. Claude saves the token. The skill continues.</li>
        <li>Authorization persists per MCP server. Every plugin that talks to that server reuses the token.</li>
      </ol>

      <h3>Custom URL (self-hosted)</h3>
      <p>Some MCP servers ship with an empty URL in <code>.mcp.json</code>: Snowflake, Databricks, Gmail, Google Calendar. These are pointers to your own instance:</p>

      <pre class="connectors-pre"><code><span class="connectors-comment"># From plugins/data/.mcp.json</span>
"snowflake":  &#123; "type": "http", "url": "" &#125;,
"databricks": &#123; "type": "http", "url": "" &#125;</code></pre>

      <p>The first time a skill needs the connector, Claude prompts for the URL. Provide your account's MCP endpoint, authorize, and Claude saves both for future use.</p>

      <h3>Local stdio (npx-installed)</h3>
      <p>One pattern uses a local MCP server that runs via <code>npx</code> on your machine: no remote auth, no API keys. The <a href="/plugins/pdf-viewer"><strong>pdf-viewer</strong></a> plugin uses this. Its <code>.mcp.json</code> declares a stdio server; <code>npx</code> auto-installs the package the first time it runs. Useful for tools that operate on your local file system.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="connectors-section" id="placeholders">
      <h2>The <code>~~category</code> placeholder pattern</h2>
      <p>
        Plugin skills don't name specific vendors. They use category placeholders:
      </p>

      <pre class="connectors-pre"><code><span class="connectors-comment"># From a sales skill's prompt:</span>
"Look up the account in ~~CRM and pull recent activity."

<span class="connectors-comment"># From a data skill:</span>
"Run the query against ~~data warehouse and return results."</code></pre>

      <p>
        <code>~~CRM</code> resolves to whatever CRM you've authorized: HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive. <code>~~data warehouse</code> resolves to Snowflake, BigQuery, or Databricks. The plugin pre-configures a default set in <code>.mcp.json</code>, but any MCP server in the right category slots in.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is what makes a plugin <strong>tool-agnostic</strong>. The same <code>/sales:call-prep</code> skill works for a HubSpot shop and a Salesforce shop without rewriting.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="connectors-section" id="standalone">
      <h2>Skills work without connectors</h2>
      <p>
        Every skill is designed to degrade gracefully. Without connectors, it falls back to web search and pasted context. <code>/sales:call-prep Acme</code> with no HubSpot connection still does web research and prep questions; the connected version pulls account history automatically.
      </p>
      <p>
        Standalone is a sane starting point. Authorize connectors as you grow into them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="connectors-section" id="swapping">
      <h2>Swapping in your own connector</h2>
      <p>
        Want to use a server Pace doesn't pre-configure? Three ways:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Authorize a different MCP server in the same category.</strong> Skills reference connectors by category (<code>~~CRM</code>), so any MCP server in that category resolves. Authorize Salesforce instead of HubSpot and the sales skills keep working.</li>
        <li><strong>Edit the plugin's <code>.mcp.json</code> locally.</strong> Add an entry, change a URL, point at your own deployment. Trade-off: you've forked the plugin and lose upstream syncs.</li>
        <li><strong>Fork the plugin for your company.</strong> Copy <code>plugins/&lt;name&gt;/</code> to <code>plugins/&lt;name&gt;-custom/</code>, edit <code>.mcp.json</code> there, register the fork in <code>marketplace.json</code>. See <a href="/docs#customizing">Customizing plugins</a> for the full pattern.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="connectors-section" id="master-catalog">
      <h2>Master catalog</h2>
      <p class="connectors-section-lede">
        Every connector category across every pace plugin. Bundled servers are pre-configured in the plugin's <code>.mcp.json</code>. Alternatives are swap-in candidates with an MCP server in the same category. The plugins column shows which plugins use each category.
      </p>

      {CONNECTOR_GROUP_ORDER.map((groupKey) => (
        grouped[groupKey].length > 0 && (
          <div class="connectors-group" id={`group-${groupKey}`}>
            <h3>{CONNECTOR_GROUP_LABELS[groupKey]}</h3>
            <div class="connectors-table" role="table">
              <div class="connectors-row connectors-row-head" role="row">
                <span role="columnheader">Category</span>
                <span role="columnheader">Bundled</span>
                <span role="columnheader">Alternatives</span>
                <span role="columnheader">Used by</span>
              </div>
              {grouped[groupKey].map((c) => (
                <div class="connectors-row" role="row">
                  <span class="connectors-cell-cat" role="cell">
                    <strong>{c.name}</strong>
                    <code>{c.placeholder}</code>
                  </span>
                  <span class="connectors-cell-bundled" role="cell">
                    {c.bundled.length > 0
                      ? c.bundled.map((s) => <span class="connectors-pill">{s}</span>)
                      : <span class="connectors-empty">(none pre-configured)</span>
                    }
                  </span>
                  <span class="connectors-cell-alts" role="cell">
                    {c.alternatives.length > 0
                      ? c.alternatives.join(', ')
                      : <span class="connectors-empty">none</span>
                    }
                  </span>
                  <span class="connectors-cell-used" role="cell">
                    {c.usedBy.map((p) => (
                      <a href={`/plugins/${p}`} class="connectors-plugin-link"><code>{p}</code></a>
                    ))}
                  </span>
                </div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        )
      ))}

      <p class="connectors-note">
        * Marks a placeholder server where the MCP URL is not yet configured upstream. Provide your own instance URL when authorizing.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SubPage>

<style>
  .connectors-page {
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .connectors-header {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .connectors-eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-forest);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .connectors-header h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-3xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .connectors-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.55;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .connectors-lede a {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .connectors-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  }
  .connectors-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-xl);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    padding-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
  }
  .connectors-section h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-md);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-top: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .connectors-section p {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .connectors-section ol {
    padding-left: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    max-width: 70ch;
  }
  .connectors-section ol li {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xs);
  }
  .connectors-pre {
    background: oklch(18% 0.015 150);
    color: oklch(92% 0.005 150);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: var(--spacing-md) 0;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .connectors-pre code {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .connectors-comment {
    color: oklch(62% 0.04 150);
  }
  .connectors-section-lede {
    font-size: var(--fs-base);
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .connectors-group {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }
  .connectors-table {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-paper-elev);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-md);
  }
  .connectors-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1.4fr 1.2fr 1.6fr;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    padding: var(--spacing-sm) var(--spacing-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-mist);
    align-items: start;
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
  }
  .connectors-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .connectors-row-head {
    background: var(--color-paper);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .connectors-cell-cat {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .connectors-cell-cat strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .connectors-cell-cat code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--color-forest);
  }
  .connectors-cell-bundled {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .connectors-pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    background: var(--color-forest-dim);
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-forest-soft);
    border-radius: 999px;
  }
  .connectors-cell-alts {
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    line-height: 1.5;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .connectors-cell-used {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .connectors-plugin-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--color-charcoal);
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out-quart);
  }
  .connectors-plugin-link code {
    background: transparent;
    border: 0;
    padding: 0;
    color: inherit;
  }
  .connectors-plugin-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-forest);
    border-bottom-color: var(--color-forest-soft);
  }
  .connectors-empty {
    color: var(--color-ash);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  .connectors-note {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--color-ash);
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 1px 7px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-code-border);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .connectors-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--spacing-xs);
    }
    .connectors-row-head {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
